---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/faq/"]}>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">
          Otto FAQs: Notes, Pricing, Tools &amp; Practice Fit
        </span>
      </nav>
      <section class="tool-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">Questions worth asking</div>
        <h1>Get a clearer picture of Otto.</h1>
        <p>Direct answers, with links to the details.</p>
      </section>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Who is Otto designed for?</summary>
          <p>
            Otto’s public site describes an AI-native EHR for mental health
            providers. Evaluate its current workflows against your practice
            size, specialty, payment model, and record requirements.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does Otto offer more than AI note drafting?</summary>
          <p>
            The public product page also lists scheduling, telehealth, patient
            records, and payments. See the{" "}
            <a href="/mental-health-ehr/">mental health EHR overview</a> for the
            workflow.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which note formats does Otto describe?</summary>
          <p>
            Otto lists SOAP and DAP notes. The clinician reviews, edits, and
            signs the draft. Read about{" "}
            <a href="/ai-progress-notes/">AI progress notes</a>.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What does the advertised trial include?</summary>
          <p>
            The current public offer is 10 signed notes or 30 days, whichever
            comes first, with no card required. Contact the{" "}
            <a href="/waitlist/">Otto team</a> to confirm billing details.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does a superbill guarantee reimbursement?</summary>
          <p>
            Payment depends on the client’s plan, benefits, deductible,
            eligibility, and submission requirements. A superbill supplies
            information for a claim. Read the{" "}
            <a href="/blog/superbill-for-therapy/">superbill guide</a>.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Are these free tools part of the EHR?</summary>
          <p>
            These are standalone browser tools. This resource site does not
            establish that the same workflows are integrated into the Otto EHR.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do the free tools upload or save my entries?</summary>
          <p>
            The tools calculate and build documents in the browser without
            submitting entries to a server or saving them in browser storage.
            Downloads and printouts contain the entered information. Use
            fictitious client details in this review version.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>
            Can I import existing records or use insurance claims?
          </summary>
          <p>
            Current support and limits need to be confirmed with Otto. Ask for a
            demonstration using the record formats, payers, and workflows your
            practice needs.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where can I review data handling and BAA terms?</summary>
          <p>
            Start with the <a href="/security/">security review questions</a>{" "}
            and request written, Otto-specific answers. This site does not
            verify BAA availability or recording-retention terms.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="cta">
          <div>
            <h2>Make more room for the work you love.</h2>
            <p>
              See how Otto brings notes, scheduling, telehealth, and payments
              into your practice day.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
            Join the waitlist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
